        "original_id": "da9b9f0a-f050-503b-9faa-afc116c283f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan Balan, T.I., Rihanna, Radu Sîrbu, Arsenie Todiraș, Jason Geter\n- Organizations: O-Zone, Grand Hustle Records\n- Products: “Live Your Life”, Paper Trail\n- Places: Moldova, Atlanta, Georgia\n\nFacts:\n- O-Zone was a Moldovan pop music trio active from 1998 to 2005, and it consisted of Dan Balan, Radu Sîrbu, and Arsenie Todiraș.\n- Grand Hustle Records, formerly Grand Hustle Entertainment and also known as Hustle Gang Music, is an Atlanta, Georgia-based record label founded in 2001 by T.I. and Jason Geter.\n- “Live Your Life” is a song by American rapper T.I. from his 2008 sixth studio album Paper Trail, and it features Barbadian singer Rihanna.\n- Dan Balan is the first and only Moldovan musician to be nominated for a Grammy as a co-writer of Rihanna and T.I.’s “Live Your Life.”",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
